622	                // extends %}` and then a variable with that named is also set
623	                // in the parent template, then you won't be able to call that
624	                // macro in the body.
625	                //
626	                // The reason for this is that blocks unlike macros do not have
627	                // closures in Jinja2/MiniJinja.
628	                //
629	                // However for the common case this is convenient because it
630	                // lets you put some imports there and for as long as you do not
